===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[fill]]s.
#* {{RQ:Mortimer Husbandry
|passage=They commonly have three, four, five, or six hewers or diggers, to four '''fillers''', so as to keep the '''fillers''' always at work.}}
# Something [[added]] to [[fill]] a [[space]] or add [[weight]] or [[size]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1977|title=Stereo Review|volume=38|page=70
|passage=I recommend this album in the face of the fact that five of the eleven songs are the purest '''filler''', dull instrumentals with a harmonica rifling over an indifferent rhythm section. The rest is magnificent{{...}}}}
# Any [[semisolid]] [[substance]] used to fill [[gap]]s, [[crack]]s or [[pore]]s.
# {{lb|en|[[cosmetic surgery]]}} A [[dermal]] filler, a substance injected beneath the skin to restore lost volume.
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Amy Synnott|quotee=Dr. Frank|title=Those Weight Loss Drugs May Do a Number on Your Face|work=w:The New York Times|date=2023-01-24|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/24/style/ozempic-weight-loss-drugs-aging.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=A 50-year-old patient will come in, and suddenly, she’s super-skinny and needs '''filler''', which she never needed before.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/dq1jO|archivedate=2023-01-24}}
# A relatively [[inert]] ingredient added to modify physical [[characteristics]]; a [[bulking agent]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2014|author=Ken Seufert|month=April|title=The New Dawn of Pharmaceutical Manufacturing: Innovative Solutions for Unprecedented Challenges|journal=American Pharmaceutical Review|section='''17'''(3):9
|passage=The word '''"filler"''' is taboo in the [[excipient]] world.}}
# A short [[article]] in a [[newspaper]] or [[magazine]].
# A short piece of [[music]] or an [[announcement]] between [[radio]] or [[TV]] [[programme]]s.
# {{senseid|en|linguistics}} {{lb|en|linguistics}} Any spoken sound or word used to fill gaps in [[speech]]; [[filled pause]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Virgil|chapter=Dedication|passage='Tis a meer '''filler'''; to ſtop a vacancy in the Hexameter, and connect the Preface to the Work of ''{{w|Virgil}}''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2007-08-24|author=William Grimes|title=Uh, Lead My Rips: No More Bloopers|work=w:The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/08/24/books/24book.html
|passage=As the years go by, speech reverts to childhood levels of disfluency, with more pauses, more errors, more repeated words, but even the peak years are not great: up to 8 percent of the average person’s word output consists of meaningless '''fillers''' and placeholders like um, uh and er.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/tERzz|archivedate=2013-01-04}}
# [[cut|Cut]] [[tobacco]] used to make up the [[body]] of a [[cigar]].
# {{lb|en|programming}} In [[COBOL]], the [[description]] of an [[unnamed]] part of a [[record]] that contains no [[data]] relevant to a given context (normally capitalised when in a [[data division]]).
# {{lb|en|horticulture}} A [[plant]] that lacks a distinctive shape and can fill inconvenient spaces around other plants in pots or gardens.
# {{lb|en|forestry|usually|in the plural}} Any standing [[tree]] or [[standard]] higher than the surrounding [[coppice]] in the form of forest known as "coppice under standards".
# {{lb|en|television|music}} material of lower cost or quality that is used to fill a certain television time slot or physical medium, such as a music album

